diff --git a/docs/harness/log.md b/docs/harness/log.md
index 3a313eb37..baa6456a2 100644
--- a/docs/harness/log.md
+++ b/docs/harness/log.md
@@ -105,3 +105,9 @@ Risks seen before the harness:
 - full-gate: Not in any gate: tools/test-integration.py and the other Python tools (they need a running server), and tests on MySQL, PostgreSQL or SQL Server (unit tests use H2 or memory only). Recorded in docs/harness/log.md.
 - local-env: debug.xml points web.path to ./traccar-web/simple, and the server stops at startup when that folder is missing (the submodule is empty in this checkout). make dev works around it with an API-only run (CONFIG_USE_ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES=true, WEB_PATH=./target/web). The web UI cannot be served locally until the submodule question is answered.
 - fast-gate: This machine has only JDK 17 (default) and Homebrew JDK 25. The gates were verified on JDK 25 through tools/harness/java-home.sh. CI uses Temurin 21. Every Gradle run also needs Maven Central, because build.gradle resolves versions at configuration time.
+
+## 2026-11-01: per-device position filter settings
+
+- What changed: `filter.invalid`, `zero`, `duplicate`, `outdated`, `future`, `past`, `accuracy`, `approximate`, `static`, `distance`, `maxSpeed`, `minPeriod`, `dailyLimit`, `dailyLimitInterval` and `skipLimit` are now `KeyType.DEVICE` keys. `FilterHandler` resolves them for each position with `AttributeUtil.lookup` (device, groups, config, key default) and is built with `new FilterHandler(cacheManager, statisticsManager)`. `filter.globalDailyLimit` and `filter.enable` stay config-only.
+- What I learned: `AttributeUtil.lookup` reads the config through `Config.getString(key)`, so tests must mock `getString`, not `getBoolean`/`getLong`. Key defaults now apply: `filter.future` defaults to 86400 s, so a "pass everything" test handler must set it to 0.
+- What is left: nothing known. The web UI may need to list the new device attributes (traccar-web submodule, not in this checkout).
